  "title": "Fix the broken lint setup",
  "type": "fix",
  "userRequest": "## Summary\n\nLint cannot start. `eslint.config.mjs` imports `eslint-config-next/core-web-vitals` and `eslint-config-next/typescript`, but the installed `eslint-config-next` is v15 while the app runs Next 16, and ESLint fails with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND before checking any file.\n\n## Key Decisions\n\n- Align `eslint-config-next` with the installed Next major version rather than rewriting the config by hand.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Bump `eslint-config-next` in `package.json` to the version matching `next`.\n- Confirm `npx eslint` runs on `app/` and `.devcontainer/codeyam-preview-origin.test.ts`, then fix any findings.",
  "description": "Lint runs again. The ESLint config package for Next.js was a major version behind the installed Next.js, so linting crashed before checking any file. It is now on the matching version, lint skips CodeYam's generated files, and lint runs as part of every build check. The few warnings it then raised were fixed: links between pages in the site header, the empty My Races message and the race-not-found page now use Next.js page links, and the filter chips mark the selected one as current instead of pressed. No screen looks different; all affected screenshots were recaptured and are pixel-identical.\n\nScope verdict: this was maintenance and delivered no product deliverable. Nothing new deferred. The one existing deferral, email/push reminders, stays deferred by the user's earlier decision. The duplicate plan about the template's lint setup is covered by this fix.",
